<p>The residential option looks $3,400 cheaper at purchase but is $2,000 ahead by month 12 and $0 ahead by month 24 — before counting the health inspection risk, the workflow drag from 120-minute cycles, and the trays you can't wash.</p>

<h2>When a Residential Dishwasher IS Okay</h2>
<p>One legitimate scenario: a residential dishwasher in the staff kitchen for employee coffee mugs, where no food production happens. That's outside the FDA Food Code's scope.</p>

<p>Anywhere food touches the equipment — bake trays, mixing bowls, utensils used to prepare product — you need NSF 3 or equivalent.</p>

